1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:05:42,750
Part 9 stopped where the calves and the friends had entered the mouth, and had not been swallowed. Entrance is of two kinds. A snake catches with the jaws and gulps. Here he did not gulp. They went straight into the mouth. The question comes, there were many thousands of children, how did they fit in that mouth. He was that vast. First the calves went ahead. After that, thousands of children. All went into the mouth. There was only entrance. They were not swallowed. They were not crushed. Aghasura was waiting for Bakari to enter. Bakari means the enemy of Baka. The killer of our brother. Shukadeva Goswami is translating his heart. He is not using the name Krishna. He is saying Bakari. When Bakari enters, then I will grind all of them at once into the body, into the belly. Until death, that demon kept remembering his dear brother and sister. They had been killed by Krishna. From this the enmity toward Krishna had grown. Until Krishna entered, he did not drop the mouth, and he did not contract the mouth. The Lord is the one who gives fearlessness to the whole universe, and for a short while he could not give fearlessness even to his own friends. This is his sweet lila. For a short time he took himself as unable. He fell into grief. He is not doing the lila in the form of the Lord. His own energy is having him do this lila. At first he could not stop them. He who frees the whole universe from fear, who gives happiness, is seeing that our own people have slipped from our hand. They have fallen from the hand. Can I not save them from Aghasura's belly. Shukadeva Goswami is speaking that same state of mind, as the Lord is thinking. All at once that child became sad. He became distressed. They have gone from our hand. The meaning is, he showed a human feeling. Now these have gone into the demon's belly. If I go, he will eat me also. They have no other protector. I alone am the protector. They are poor. In our heart the pain will stay just like this. Now their death will happen. In the flame of Aghasura's belly they have become straw, they have become grass. As you put straw into a forest fire, the straw burns. Inside there was great heat. In everyone's belly there is some heat, and by that same fire food is digested. The fire of Aghasura's belly was blazing. The children will die as soon as they go. He became very sad. By mercy the mind filled. Because of love for the children, in a short time he thought all of this.

2
00:05:42,750 --> 00:09:44,490
Now what shall I do. What shall I do so that this wicked one dies, his life does not remain, and our friends are saved. They had gone into the belly. They have gone into a snake's mouth. The snake has to die. Killing the snake, the children who have gone into the belly have to be saved. What is to be done here. Let the wicked one's life be destroyed, and let these good people not be killed. For a short while he fell into worry. After that the decision came at once. It is the energy of his own form. The Lord is the Supreme Lord. Saying this, he himself went to enter Aghasura. Tell me a courage of this kind. If a python has caught someone, which man will go into its mouth himself. He went to save his own children. One acharya has written on this feeling that the Lord thought, if death must come, all will die together. The Lord can never die. A thought of this kind cannot rise in his mind. But in the lila he can think anything. Love toward those children is being shown. He entered. He keeps his eye on all. He understood both things, this one will also die, and our companions will also be saved. This is called the seer of everything, with nothing left out. One acharya makes one meaning, that without Shesha means he has not come with Shesha. Balarama is the avatara of Shesha. He did not bring Shesha. If he had come bringing Balarama, he would never have let these children enter. Balarama would have known that this is a python. Those who live having taken the form of a snake understand all the ways of a snake. The children are saying, this is a mountain, it is looking like a python. Balarama would say at once, is this a python or a stone. Come, move. He would not let them go. Then the lila would not have happened. Here Krishna is called the seer with nothing left out. There is no time, no person, no inner mind, that remains outside his sight. He sees everywhere. He understands all. Then he, the seer of all, entered. He did not go fully into the belly. When he entered the mouth, the gods were watching this sight from behind the clouds.

3
00:09:46,240 --> 00:14:52,150
They could not fly the airplanes in the open. Otherwise Kamsa would give them great pain. From fear of Kamsa they were all behind the clouds. When the Lord entered Aghasura's mouth, the gods began to cry ha ha on their airplanes. Suddenly, from grief. They could not stop themselves. The Lord heard an unclear sound. Everyone knows. The gods are the Lord's great devotees, and they know his opulence. They know that Krishna is the Supreme Lord. But because they are devotees, there is love in the mind. Where there is love, there is the fear of harm to the beloved. And however many kinsmen Aghasura had, his sons, brothers, relatives, Kamsa and the rest, they became greatly delighted. The gods began to weep. Seeing this sight, they began to cry out. And the demons, Aghasura's relatives, became greatly delighted. A question rises, how did they come to know. The gods were watching in front, so they became unhappy. How did these people become delighted. These are all great scientists. They had set up an arrangement of news. As soon as the entrance happened, just as someone might see it on a television, so they saw it. Among the demons there was an arrangement of this kind. All saw that Krishna is going into the mouth, and they became greatly delighted. They clapped a great deal. They began to shout victory. Or one meaning has been made, that this is the very nature of demons. When trouble falls on the world, their auspicious limbs begin to twitch. The right limbs twitch. In the commentary, Srila Sanatana Goswami says, or, as they keep the news, so they will have kept it. However it was, they came to know. And all became delighted. Because it was being sent. At that time all were seated. The news spread at once, that Krishna has entered Aghasura's mouth. They began to play the congratulations. They became very pleased. The Lord heard both these sounds. One he heard with the ear. He also heard the grief-tone of the gods. He heard the pitiful crying. He heard the ha ha. To console Maharaj Pariksit, Shukadeva Goswami says, fearless. Sri Krishna is fearless. Not even a hair of his can be bent. The opulence is equal in every way. There is no loss. There is no cause for worry. When he went into the throat, at that same time the snake began the effort, to drop them, to close his own mouth. Now Krishna has come into his mouth. The children had already come. He wanted to close the mouth slowly. The Lord saw, he wants to crush us. The Lord is fearless. He cannot be crushed. But the effort to crush began.

4
00:14:52,690 --> 00:19:34,240
So far that even breathing, or sending the inner breath out, was not possible for him. Closing completely, like rubber, they shrank in it, they stuck. They jammed completely. There was no hole anywhere by which anyone could breathe. He grew suddenly. He expanded himself with speed in the throat. What had been made a python became a real python. Today they jammed in his throat. Although I am unborn, and my body is imperishable, although I am the Lord of all beings. [Bhagavad-gita 4.6] The Lord himself says, I am unborn. The unborn has gone into the python. He has gone into the throat. One in whose throat a goat jams is called a python. This is the definition. That serpent who swallows one goat, one goat who passes through his throat, is called a python. A goat is called aja. But the real aja, the unborn, is Lord Krishna. A question comes. When he killed Bakasura, when he killed Putana, at that time he had not expanded the body. Why did he expand it this time. Could he not kill in another way. Srila Vishvanatha Chakravarti Thakur says, the Lord thought, at this time there is no one watching, so let me become large and kill. At another time people are watching. In front of the residents of Braj he cannot become large. In front of them everything has to be done while remaining a tiny child. Here no one was watching. So he grew at once. He manifested his opulence. In front of the residents of Braj he does not manifest his opulence. Perhaps this can be one cause. The snake began to thrash. From the head, the whole inside, every inch, had jammed in the throat. He had a very vast body, and still the whole throat was filled with Krishna. The path was blocked. The sight turned completely over. The eyes came out. He began to thrash here and there. He began to be bewildered. In the inner body the wind was blocked. The wind filled. It was not coming out. That same wind broke his head and came out. The life came out from the crown. It came out from the head. Breaking it like that. A very large part of the head of his body suddenly split and went separate. It is not that someone stays stuck in the body. It is not that some yogi will leave the body. Yogis leave the body by meditating. And one inside whose body the Lord has gone, how much meditation is happening for him. So the life came out from the crown. And by that all the life-breaths came out. First the wind came out, and with it all the consciousness went. No body was working. That is, he died.

5
00:19:34,240 --> 00:23:30,630
When he had died, then the Lord entered his belly. There all the children, first from separation from Krishna, and second from the flame of his belly, all had fainted. They had died. Or they had burned, fainted, and fallen. Here the word for the dead is written. They had died. From the flame of the poison, from that serpent demon. The children also had died inside. The Lord brought all back to life. The children, and his own companions. Then, together with them, he came out by the mouth. They did not come out by the crown. As they had entered, so they came out. And on the bodies of all the children there was no shelter of a wound in any direction. There was nothing. He lifted them with his own glance. There was no need to put the hand. With the glance of his own compassion he brought all back to life. This is the meaning. Many times the Lord has brought the residents of Braj back to life with his glance. From the flame of the poison of the Kaliya serpent, the cowherd men had also died once. He brought them back to life. Here he brought them back to life. In the Lord's glance nectar dwells. The moon also came out from the glance, and it is called the maker of nectar. When the moon that came from the Lord's eye is the maker of nectar, then how much nectar will be in the eye. With nectar, with the deathless drink, he brought them to life. The meaning is, he brought them to life with the glance of affection. From the mouth, Mukunda came out. On this an acharya has made a very beautiful poetic fancy. Shukadeva Goswami is saying the word Mukunda. I want to say it here after reading that. Only the word Mukunda came. However many names the Lord has, they have some fixed meanings. They are meaningful names. True to the sense. However many names I have, all are meaningful. They are famous on the earth. But here he freed his own people, his kinsmen, from Aghasura, and he freed Aghasura himself from the bondage of the world. Here it seems he wants to manifest his name Mukunda completely. One who frees, who gives liberation, is called Mukunda. He freed the children from Aghasura. He freed Aghasura from the bondage of the world. Shukadeva Goswami is giving the name Mukunda here. Having caught the Lord's intention.

6
00:23:35,510 --> 00:27:41,140
Now the soul came out. First the life-breath had come out of the body. There is a difference between the life-breath and the soul. From the body of that very thick serpent a wonderful light came out. A great light. In this world we do not see a light like the light that came out. With its own radiance it lit the ten directions. And it waited in the sky. When Lord Krishna had come out of Aghasura's mouth, that light, while the gods were watching, entered him. The gods were all watching. With eyes that did not blink. Their eyelids do not fall in that way either. They were watching the Lord's lila. Aghasura attained the Lord. He became Krishna's attendant, in the eternal lila. Like Putana. This is a very wonderful thing. The Lord has described the soul in the Gita. The soul of everyone does leave the body. But having left the body, where it went, nothing is known. Not only theirs. Of the great yogis also, of the devotees also, where the soul went, nothing is known. Let it go to Vaikuntha, but in what form it is going is not seen. After that, by the Lord's wish, it came out shining in the form of light, and then it entered the Lord. He showed it in front of all. One acharya says, the name of the sky is the place of Vishnu's feet. Why did that soul stay a short while in the place of Vishnu's feet. He says, Aghasura is as if saying, look, even a sinner like me, having come in contact with the Lord's body, has been freed today. And look, I am telling the truth. Any person can be freed. I am saying it while touching Vishnu's feet. In this way he is as if declaring it. He is saying it while touching the place of Vishnu's feet. Staying in the place of Vishnu's feet. And then he entered Krishna. A wonderful thing happened. Our acharyas write, why did it happen like this. Why did that soul not go quietly to Goloka. Why was it shown somewhere. The secret of this is, the Lord wanted to show it. Aghasura's light came out and was absorbed in the Lord.

7
00:27:48,290 --> 00:31:20,880
When Aghasura had died, had been absorbed in the Lord, then the gods began to serve the Lord. Those who play instruments began to play loudly. They began to sing. They began to praise. Who was doing what, Shukadeva Goswami describes. The gods became exceedingly delighted at that time. Because the Lord had done their work, by killing one wicked one. They became very pleased. They began to rain flowers on Krishna. They began to rain the flowers of the Nandana forest, of the Chaitraratha forest, of the Sarvatobhadra forest. The apsaras began to dance. Those who sing beautiful songs began to sing. Those who hold instruments began to play. The brahmanas began to praise. And the Lord's associates who had come in the sky began to shout victory. One acharya asks a question on this, why the instruments and the rest of all of them were not described together. Why it is being done separately. Then he says, the gods are so pleased that they thought, if we do it all mixed together, this is not right. The right the Lord has given us, the facility he has given, we will offer separately in the Lord's service. So those who sing beautiful songs sang. Those who rain flowers rained. The apsaras danced. Whatever capacity each had, he offered it in the Lord's service. The instrument that played in that world, in heaven, such beautiful instruments, and so many praises, began to be wonderful. So great a festival happened. Song, instrument, distributing sweets, all. All of this began in a very large form. And the sound of the festival spread so far that the sound went into Brahma's world. Brahma heard, what is happening. Why is it happening like this. What kind of sound is it. He comes and sees.

8
00:31:22,380 --> 00:35:52,570
Brahma came. Simply by seeing Aghasura's liberation he became greatly astonished. And on this, in order to see the charming glory of the Lord, he will steal the calves and the children. Now see, a new lila of these is about to begin. When the Lord had wiped their written account, on this Brahma was becoming somewhat angry. They do so much sin, and the Lord sends them to Vaikuntha. Then what was the need of the labor I have done. He was a little displeased even with his own father. Meaning, with the Lord. This was one cause. So in the course of the talk he will steal the calves, let us see what he does now. He wants to see one more glory. One acharya says, to make him an associate, this is the Lord's glory. Killing him would not have been their glory. To give him liberation, to give release, this is the Lord's glory. On this they became full of wonder. They became astonished. How great the Lord is. There was also a little anger. Making him an associate is not only this much. The body he had, the body leaving which he was freed, that body also remained in Vrindavan as a plaything of conscious substance. As when Putana's body was burned, because the Lord had drunk the milk of her breast, for this reason Putana's body had become divine. When it was burned, the fragrance of aguru came from it. Smoke spread on all four sides through the whole circle of Braj. The residents of Braj smelled it. Whereas the smell of a pyre is very bad. No one wants to smell it. His vast body dried later. It dried. But for the children it remained a cave just the same, a road just the same, everything. And later they would come and play a great deal of hide and seek. They would slide. And all would say, this has become a thing for playing.

9
00:35:59,910 --> 00:40:36,520
Aghasura's body remained as one limb of Vrindavan. As Giriraj is, in that way. O king, O Maharaj Pariksit, that dried body of the python remained for a long time in Vrindavan as a cave of play for those children. A cave. Into his body they would go kos after kos, inside. They would keep playing. This is mercy. See the Lord's. The body in which the Lord had entered, had it remained beyond matter. For a long time the children kept playing in it. It worked as a cave for play. For hiding, here and there. The children would enter far into that darkness. They would play. Someone would speak while staying here. He would speak loudly. He would call, in a very sweet tone. I am here. I am here. Find me. They would go into the darkness. He is not seen. And outside also they would slide on his body. They would wander. They would throw themselves. See this, the good fortune. The effect of contact with the Lord. A material body of this kind cannot be. But one whom the Lord touches, inside whom he goes, what is rare for him. This lila had happened in the kumara age. But the children will go and tell it in Braj in the pauganda age, that he freed us from the snake. A snake had swallowed us. We had died. But Krishna saved us. They will say it after going, a year later. This is becoming the occasion of a question. Where were they for this year. How did it happen like this. This question will be asked tomorrow. The lila done in the kumara age, the children told after going into the pauganda age. Its meaning is, this lila had happened at the beginning of the fifth year, and the children, at the beginning of the sixth year, will go and tell it to their mothers, to everyone. This question will be tomorrow. Now this is being considered. When Aghasura was liberated, became the Lord's associate, in their eternal Braj lila, and his body remained as the beauty of this Vrindavan, remained as one limb, in which the children would play. Maharaj Pariksit fell into wonder. The sages who were seated, hearing the katha, all made a face of this kind, so that it seemed to Shukadeva Goswami that all are wondering. He has said a wonderful thing. Such fortune for Aghasura.

10
00:40:44,120 --> 00:47:55,970
What are you people wondering at. Whose lila are you hearing. Consider this. Lord Sri Krishna is a human child. He is the son of Nanda Maharaj. And he is possessed of maya. The meaning of maya is mercy. Joined with mercy. Merciful. Compassionate. In truth he is the Lord of all, small or great. He is able to do all. He is the maker of all the arrangements. Whose destination will be what, who should receive what, he is the giver of everything. And all together, he is kind. He is one whose heart is in very great mercy. So he did not consider Aghasura's heart. His wickedness, the inner mind, and his decision, the Lord never brought into his own mind. He only saw this, that this one is taking me inside his own body. So by Krishna's touch all of Aghasura's sins were destroyed. Shattered. And so he attained the friendship of the self. The Lord's associate. He became their friend. Of the friends he had wanted to eat, he became one. He became a friend. This gift was given, which is very rare for the untrue. Extremely rare. Even for a saint it is rare. The untrue is a far talk. Saints cannot obtain this destination. What was given. Why it happened like this. Then he is saying it by the logic of how much more. When only a deity is made of Lord Krishna's form, of the Lord's beautiful limbs, and someone remembers even that deity in the mind, and that also only once, then he attains the destination of the Lord. With the mind. A deity. As Govindadeva is, or Madan-gopal, Madan-mohan, or Krishna-Balarama, Banke Bihari. It is a deity of the Lord. In one way, he is that also. Where the Lord is, there that person goes, having become his associate, by meditating on the form. And that also once. One by whose form's meditation a person can go near the Lord, can become an associate, that same Lord in person, condensed supreme bliss, and supreme opulence. The destination was received. What wonder is this. The point is, all were astonished, how did it happen like this. And of the Lord's deity, not the whole, even one hand, even his finger, if it is remembered, and even once, still the Lord's destination is received. And then if the whole body is coming into remembrance in the mind, from the feet to the toenail and the crown, all the ornament, even once with the mind, then he attains the Lord's destination. And if somewhere he is remembering many times with the mind, then more. Not with the mind, if he is seeing with the eye, then what destination will there be, tell me. And he is seeing with the eye, he is ornamenting him, he is offering food, he is singing a song to please him. Why would the Lord's destination not come to him. This rule Shukadeva Goswami is telling himself. This Bhagavatam is the greatest book that nourishes the principle. This Bhagavatam alone, in truth, tells the real devotion. Here, how much importance the seeing of the Lord's deity, the worship, the remembrance, holds, this has been told. And in truth the Lord is not in the form of a deity. He is the son of the king of Vraja in person. Chaitanya Mahaprabhu says this. The worship that happens in the temples, in truth the Lord appears and accepts his own worship and adoration. [Chaitanya-charitamrita] But with that eye he will not understand. With the eye of scripture, with the Bhagavatam's eye, the thing comes. In truth he is manifest in the beautiful form. Even by meditating on such a form, on the deity, even once, when the Lord's destination can be received.

11
00:47:55,970 --> 00:54:52,380
This is the Lord's nature. He had entered with the whole limb. Will some yogi meditate. He will die while meditating. The Lord does not come even in the mind. And one this fortunate, into whose heart the Lord himself went. He did not go alone. With his own friends also, and with the calves, all went. Then why would he not be freed. So Lord Krishna should be remembered. He should be seen. By itself the living being will be freed. And by pronouncing his name the living being attains the Lord's destination. Then the talk of the deity is farther still. It is a very important verse. I am finishing it by saying it very quickly. But this is only one or two verses. They should be kept for one day's katha. Let it be. But now the katha is growing. A great deal has remained. So we close here. Tomorrow. Hidden in the answer is where they were for a year. That they had forgotten, and the memory came after a year. No. They had not gone home at all for a year. The real thing. Brahma will steal the children in between. Hare Krishna. Glory to Srila Prabhupada. When the lila of Brahma's bewilderment is coming. Om bhagavate vasudevaya. Om namo bhagavate vasudevaya. Suta said. In this katha Vedavyasa is saying, is writing. He is saying, Suta said. Maharaj Pariksit, hearing the katha of Aghasura's bondage and of Aghasura's good destination, was greatly moved. Great joy came to him. Hearing this nature of the Lord, his lila, he asks a question in the middle. The cause of the question was that Srila Shukadeva Goswami had said, this lila done in the kumara age, the release from the serpent. The children will go in the pauganda age and say it in Braj. The lila that had happened at the beginning of the fifth year, the children will go at the beginning of the sixth year and tell it in Braj. What all they will tell. About that he says, how they had been freed from the serpent by Krishna. And how Krishna, having gone into the throat, freed them. All those things the children will go and tell in the sixth year. On this Maharaj Pariksit is asking. What Maharaj Pariksit is. How his mind is seized in Krishna-katha. This, Suta Goswami is telling to the sages beginning with Shaunaka, in Naimisharanya. About Maharaj Pariksit, Suta says, given by the God of the Yadus. The God of the Yadus, the worshipful, the dear Sri Krishna. He had given Maharaj Pariksit. When Drona's son Ashvatthama attacked Uttara's womb with the brahmastra, the Lord entered the womb and protected that infant. And by protecting, in one way he gave a son to Maharaj Yudhishthira, or he gave him to Uttara, he saved him. So he was called given. Maharaj Pariksit, protected in the womb, had been given by the God of the Yadus, to Uttara and to Yudhishthira. Therefore. His own matter came back to Maharaj Pariksit. As the Lord protected the calves and the keepers of the calves from Aghasura's belly, in the same way the Lord had also protected me in my mother's womb. In the mind a matching of the two lilas came at once. These children were protected in Aghasura's belly, and Maharaj Pariksit was protected in his mother's womb. On hearing the katha, that matter was remembered. So the word given by the God of the Yadus was used. That same event began to be remembered, that the Lord had protected us in the womb, had saved us. So, having heard the wonderful character of his own protector, he asks again about the same. What he has already heard, about the same he is asking again. Or connected with the same. Why is he asking. Srila Shukadeva Goswami gives its answer. He says, the mind is seized. Seized from birth. The lilas of the child Krishna have caught it. The mind had become stuck in Krishna's lila. Seized utterly. Fully, his mind was attached to the Lord's lilas. Not that he seized the lilas. The Lord had seized Maharaj Pariksit's mind. In the Bhagavatam this has been said. Srila Shukadeva Goswami's mind also, not that he had seized the Lord's lilas. He had not seized the lilas. The lilas themselves would come and attract the mind. The beautiful lila of the unconquered one had drawn the essence. And Shukadeva Goswami himself says.

12
00:54:53,790 --> 01:00:15,690
It is in the opening verses of the second canto. My mind seized, O royal sage, I studied this account. Seeing all of this, I am forgetting. How is the whole. When Shukadeva Goswami said that at the end of Dvapara I studied this Bhagavatam from my father, Maharaj Pariksit says, you are completely renounced, a forest-dweller, and completely without longing. Full in desire. A sage who rejoices in the self. How did you study so large a book. Then he says, the lila of the one whose verses are the highest seized my mind. And so I studied. In this way, here also about Maharaj Pariksit, Suta Goswami says, the mind seized. The childhood lilas of Krishna had attracted Maharaj Pariksit's mind. Seized means, had brought it under their own control. Leaving the thought of the Lord's lilas, Maharaj Pariksit's mind cannot go anywhere else at all. A person who has been caught, who has been bound, how can he go. So Maharaj Pariksit was hearing the katha of his own protector, of his supremely dear one, of his worshipful Lord. With that Krishna whose katha Maharaj Pariksit is hearing, he had a very near relation. First, the relation of his grandfathers. That same Lord today has protected thousands of children, has protected the calves. So, hearing this katha, the memory of that event came. After the war of the Mahabharata, his own protection had happened. So, drawn by the katha, he asked again. About that childhood play. Holy. That same holy account, which frees the soul from every kind of ignorance and gives love for the Lord, is called holy. An act done after an interval of time. The work that was done one year before, how did it become of that moment. It is an act done at a different time. How did it become of that moment at another time. The children will go, a year later, and say that today the son of Nanda killed Aghasura. They will say so. Then how did an act done after an interval become of that moment. When those children were speaking, how did it become of that time. What was done after an interval, became of the moment. So it is said, what Hari did in the kumara age, the children of the pauganda age will go and tell. These are children. Children will not lie. Children are very simple in this way. Then how did it happen that they go into Braj and say of an event one year old, today he killed Aghasura, Krishna took us out of the belly. O great yogi, guru, in this question we have a great curiosity. He is addressing him as guru twice. To hear this we have a great longing. Why did those children not tell their mothers this event for one year. In truth this is a matter of curiosity. For one year, what were they doing. Where were they.

13
01:00:15,690 --> 01:09:34,540
Certainly this will be some energy of Hari alone. Another thing cannot be. The meaning of maya is energy. It will be some energy of the Lord alone. But he is saying maya because these children will have been put into bewilderment. They will have been put into confusion. Only then would they tell a lila done a year back, in the next year, as if the event has happened now. The event has happened today. Certainly it will be some special energy of Sri Krishna. Since the children have been put into confusion. Supremely charming. Attracting all. Condensed supreme bliss. This word should be understood as we go. Why the word Hari is being given. In the verse above also, done by Hari. And here also Maharaj Pariksit is saying, this is Hari's energy alone, not another's. That on those children any energy other than Krishna's should work, this I cannot accept. Eternally liberated. They are the Lord's associates. They are his company. So these are not under the great illusion. And for this reason the energy of any god, of a yaksha, of a demon, or of anyone, does not work on them. Having done it, please tell us. And confirming the Krishna-katha heard before, he says, we are the most fortunate in the world, O guru, though low kshatriyas, because again and again we drink from you the holy nectar of Krishna-katha. A talk of this kind. Maharaj Pariksit about himself. From drinking the nectar, the supreme bliss is being received. In this absorption Maharaj Pariksit says, in this world, in this universe, I alone am the most fortunate person. Fortunate is said of one who has wealth. That person who is now going to die within three days, whom the snake Takshaka is going to bite, that person is saying that in this universe I am the most fortunate. Self-praise, one's own glory, one's own magnification, is not done. But in truth Maharaj Pariksit felt so. In this universe there is no other. We. He is putting it in the plural. The intention of the word we is that whoever is hearing the katha, all are as fortunate as I am. Or, being the disciple of Srila Shukadeva Goswami, he takes himself as great, and the word we. By drinking the nectar of the katha, more fortunate. By drinking again and again, most fortunate. Only by being your disciple we are fortunate. And on that the nectar of Krishna-katha is being received, so we are more fortunate. It is being received again and again, so we are the most fortunate. Srila Jiva Goswami writes this. So in this universe, in truth, the greatest gain, the greatest attainment, of a living being is this, that Krishna's talks come to him to hear. From this sentence of Maharaj Pariksit it was proved. Otherwise, after only three days. The session was going on there. Maharaj Pariksit had heard only seven days. This was the fourth day of the Bhagavatam going. According to that, the fourth or the fifth, something like that. He had three days to live. And a dreadful snake, Takshaka, is going to bite him. But that person, having received Krishna-katha, is praising his fortune. In the full assembly. A low kshatriya. Although we are a low kshatriya. Not even one excellent kshatriya. Not even an equal kshatriya. Here the meaning of kshatra-bandhu is a low kshatriya. He has taken birth in a kshatriya family. But here the meaning of bandhu is low. Maharaj Pariksit is calling himself low. If I see my own act. A great sage was meditating. He threw a snake on his neck. He has great regret toward his own former act. But to such a great offender, meaning, I am saying it according to his feeling. I am not making him an offender. Then even such a one, the most fortunate. Ah, we are the most fortunate in the world. Guru, even while being low kshatriyas. What a fortune is yours. Why your fortune is great. Because from you I am drinking the nectar of Krishna-katha. From a great devotee like you, a man whose life is Krishna, I am drinking Krishna's katha. So my fortune is very great. These are all standard sentences of the Bhagavatam. Here and there they tell who in this world is in truth fortunate, and for what we should make effort. What thing we should obtain. The same katha that we people are hearing here, are speaking. Hearing this same katha, Maharaj Pariksit says that I am completely the most fortunate. Well, for the katha from the start to the end, they are saying. The katha that began from the second canto, from there up to now, for all these things he says, from your mouth, which I am drinking again and again.

