01:09:36,010 --> 01:15:02,770
He gives Krishna's message. He gives Krishna's katha. And the disciple receives it. This is the real relation. The relation of guru and disciple is very intimate. Very intimate. And what is the ground. It is on Krishna's ground. Because of Krishna. Although I am a low kshatriya. Srila Prabhupada writes, a student and a disciple has the right to ask the guru about any confidential service. A disciple has the full right that he can ask his guru any hidden thing, about the Lord. And it is also the guru's duty that he explain it, make it understood. So, addressing him twice with the word guru, Maharaj Pariksit is saying this, that I am your surrendered disciple. Although this is a confidential thing. I have understood. Because you did not say it. You are closing it here itself. So I have understood that this is a confidential thing. It is a secret. But still you are my guru. I am surrendered to you. Please, by mercy, let us hear this. Hearing this question, Shukadeva Goswami at once entered samadhi. Then that sight was remembered by him. He began to remember those things. When the Lord himself has become the cowherd boys, has become the calves, and was driving himself by himself into Braj, from Braj into the forest, for one year. That lila was remembered. He was lost in those lilas, fully in Vrindavan. Then he was awakened. By loud kirtan. By playing jhanj, mridanga, and the rest. Then Suta Goswami, who was seeing it with his own eye. Suta Goswami and Maharaj Pariksit, these two were very near. Suta Goswami has heard, and he says, by his grace I heard that katha. I was sitting right near him. The meaning is, Shukadeva Goswami had said to him, come, sit here. So he was sitting near. In front, among the hearers. Suta Goswami was seeing all, what condition came upon Shukadeva Goswami on hearing Maharaj Pariksit's question. He says, thus questioned, that son of Badarayana, all his senses were taken by that memory. With great difficulty he again obtained the outer sight. And he replied. O best of the devotees. It is an address for Shaunaka. How beautiful a thing it is. He is speaking. Srila Suta Goswami is addressing Shaunaka. O best of the bhagavatas. O best. O best of all even among the great devotees. For Shaunaka. Matching Maharaj Pariksit's eagerness and Shaunaka's eagerness, then Suta Goswami is saying the thing. As much insistence Maharaj Pariksit had for Krishna-katha, just the same insistence Shaunaka had. Rather, Shaunaka's was more than that. These people, leaving the sacrifice, rejecting it, leaving a sacrifice already begun, became ready for Krishna-katha. They say their fitness, we have the full time for the katha. For the katha of Hari. We have the full opportunity for the katha. In the world, what do people think. Let us do the work and the business. If a little time is found, then let us do the satsang. If a little time remains, then let us do the satsang. No. They want to hear the katha. And if a little time remains, then let us do the housework. This has been accepted as the standard. Best is the one who stays steeped in Krishna-katha. Who has this much insistence for hearing Krishna's talk. Then in truth he alone is the best of the bhagavatas. This is one indication. It is the standard. In truth, as much as a person is attached to Krishna's lilas, that much he is excellent.

