01:15:28,520 --> 01:20:57,360
Sri Krishna's lilas began to be remembered. Here the word unending is given for Sri Krishna. The meaning of unending, of whom there was no counting. How many he had become. In what number he had become calves, and in what number cowherd boys. Along with that he had also become their garland. The turban. The cloth. Their stick. Their lunch basket. The Lord had become everything. The food that had been placed, everything. The children had not eaten yet. Everything the same. All this is indeed Brahman. [the Veda] The universe is all pervaded by Vishnu. Shukadeva Goswami will say later that the word of the Veda came true, rightly. All had become pervaded by Vishnu. So for this reason the word unending here. When the mind, which in truth is the chief, when the mind had gone fully into Krishna's lila, then the outer tracking was not there. His eyes stayed open as they were open. But he was not seeing. The mind had gone fully inside. And so the movements of all the senses had also gone. In this way he became still. Hearing the question, the mind was absorbed in Krishna's lila. Then what should be done now. Srila Vishvanatha Chakravarti Thakur says, Maharaj Pariksit had fallen into great regret and was restless. For drinking the nectar. Then a means was made. There some sages indicated that kirtan should begin. By that sound, by the sound of jhanj, kartal, mridanga, and the rest, his mind would come out. So kirtan began. Kirtan happened very loudly. After this, in time, slowly their mental movement came outside. That I am on the bank of the Ganga. And I have to let the katha be heard. This event has come. Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare. Hare Rama, Hare Rama, Rama Rama, Hare Hare. See, how much there is that is worth learning. He is getting so bound in the Lord that he has to be brought outside. Here it sometimes happens that some people fall asleep. They have to be brought back into memory, that you have come to hear the katha. Stay awake. There is a great difference. In the katha of that time, and in your katha, there is a great difference. Then sometimes people ask, we are hearing katha, we are speaking, still why is our improvement not happening. We have fallen from the standard. We have gone very far down. So that fruit is not coming in front. That hearer and that speaker were someone else. In truth, now the speaker stays a speaker. Those who sleep, sleep. The speaker became a speaker, and the hearer became a sleeper. He is making a joke like that. See that speaker, who as soon as the question was made became completely absorbed. In the Vrindavan lila. With great difficulty he again obtained the outer sight. When the sankirtan began, the Lord's quality began to be sung, and that same lila was being sung by whose memory Shukadeva Goswami's mind was fixed in samadhi. That same lila was being sung. So that lila was able to draw his mind outside. That also with great difficulty. With hardship. With great pain Shukadeva Goswami was able to remove his mind from there. The meaning of removing the mind from there is that in his mind he also remembered, Pariksit has to be allowed to hear. This is the meaning. It is not that he forgot the lila completely and then the outer sight was obtained. Slowly. That also slowly. All at once his outer movement did not happen. It took some time, in coming outside.

