01:20:57,360 --> 01:26:44,800
After this he spoke. Srila Shukadeva Goswami welcomes this feeling of Maharaj Pariksit. Well asked. Today you asked very well. O greatly fortunate one. O best of the devotees. In one verse there are two addresses for Maharaj Pariksit. O greatly fortunate one. As Maharaj Pariksit said about himself, that we are the most fortunate, fortunate above all, so Srila Shukadeva Goswami also says, in truth you are greatly fortunate. Toward Krishna-katha your taste is this deep. So you are the best of the devotees. Well asked. You asked me a very good question. It was asked so well that he entered samadhi. And now, before giving the answer of that question, he says, you have asked very well. One should learn to ask a question, in truth. Raising a finger, and saying I have one question, by doing that the thing is spoiled. The question should be about the Lord. When the speaker says, yes, you have asked very well. A fashion of asking questions has started. Some people think that a question must happen, whatever it is. Let anything be asked. But a question should be asked at the end of the katha. If a question is not asked, it felt as if the katha itself did not happen. Once I had spoken a katha. I had taken a class somewhere. Some one or two devotees had heard. Someone said, we can ask a question. I said, no. What question is forming. What will you ask in this. At the end, the question they wanted to ask had no touch with it. So in truth the question should be about the Lord. And to nourish the thing you are hearing. In support of it. Not so that what the speaker said for half an hour or forty-five minutes is cut down. It should not be so. What someone labored for an hour and spoke, the question shatters that same idea. O greatly fortunate one, from the beginning you have been the object of Sri Krishna's mercy. The Lord has had great affection toward you. Then, going into your mother's womb, he protected you. And at this time also, giving inspiration in my heart, he wants to free you from the bondage of the world. He wants to take you into his own abode. So at the time of birth also there was the same mercy of the Lord. And at this time of death you have no panic. Nor any agitation. Your mind is fixed on Krishna in this way. You are certainly greatly fortunate. And you are the best of the devotees. Among all the devotees of the Lord you are the best. Because of being a rasika of katha. Taking Krishna-katha with this much insistence. So you are the best among the bhagavatas. You are greatly fortunate for this, and you are the best of all among the bhagavatas for this, that you are making Krishna-katha new. New means fresh. Fresh even while hearing. The katha you have already heard, even the heard katha, you are making daily new.

