Here in the world many people hear katha. And if some speaker is saying it again, they say, this is a thing already heard. Please tell some new thing. Hearing Maharaj Pariksit's question, Shukadeva does not say, you have already heard it. You did not ask any new thing. The longing to hear the same thing again is growing. So this is called, you make it new. They are making it daily new. They are making the katha daily fresh. Well, not once. Even having heard again and again. That same childhood character Maharaj Pariksit heard in many chapters. Even hearing again and again, you are making that katha daily fresh. You are blessed. And in truth you are the crest jewel among the devotees of Lord Krishna. The best of all. To say a beautiful word to someone in private, to praise him, is another thing. But in the middle of the assembly, to greet Maharaj Pariksit in this way, to magnify him in this way, is a very great thing. Best of the devotees. And greatly fortunate. So there you are hearing, Srila Suta Goswami has called Shaunaka the best of the devotees. And Shukadeva Goswami is calling Maharaj Pariksit the best of the devotees. In truth, between the speaker and the hearer of the Bhagavatam there is not a great distance. Suta Goswami was doing kirtan. Maharaj Pariksit was doing hearing. Hearing and chanting. Both were doing devotion. One who will be on one level, on one ground, he alone can take the other. He can initiate him. So as Maharaj Pariksit is a great devotee, so is Shukadeva Goswami. His nature is the same as yours. You are blessed, Maharaj. You are like the vitas. Vita is said of a man greedy for women. Who stays overly attached to women. Who takes a woman alone as the greatest aim of his life. And who feels, we have obtained a woman. Seeing the hearer, it is coming back to Srila Shukadeva Goswami, how greedy he is in Krishna-katha. As the vita people stay greedy for women. On this occasion that example began to be remembered by him. You are blessed. You are greedy for Krishna-katha like a man greedy for women. This memory came. Otherwise how could he give an example this low. Srila Vishvanatha Chakravarti Thakur says, this example of the greedy man, although the vita people get tired of talk of this kind. They do not want to hear all the time. There are many hearers. Then among the hearers, those who are attached to women, who are greedy, for however long, and with however much eagerness, they want to hear talk of women, only that comparison was found, by Shukadeva Goswami. In the world no one else listens that much. This is a strange kind. If you go to the railway station. This sitting stops here.
